            "title": "What is Creative Coding?",
            "body": "<p>Creative Coding, i.e. &quot;Creative Coding&quot;, I would like to define as a type of software that pushes the limits of the user&#39;s imagination in the web world and where the limits of each project are based on the imagination of the coder. I don&#39;t think there is a field in the universe where science and art are not together. Decisively, however, when these two great philosophies come together, there are really tremendously impressive results. If you have read Walter Isaacson, you know his views on science and art. &ldquo;Innovation is found where art and science meet, it is not new,&quot; Isaacson said.&rdquo; he says. &quot;When Einstein couldn&#39;t make much progress trying General Relativity, he would take out his violin and play a piece from Mozart, until he connected with the phase he called &lsquo;Harmony of the Spheres&rsquo;..&rdquo; With the development of science and technology, our brain and imagination are also developing, and then the designs that can affect us in the digital world should also be strengthened. Although people are used to reading in the F-Shaped Line, I think that our characteristics of this style have improved in the digital environment and the impressiveness of classic content writing has decreased. Of course, it is possible to say that it is not only a thought, but also an observation.. Creative Coding, on the other hand, is not something new, it is a coding solution that develops with us and comes to the forefront as we develop. Creative Coding is an organism that wants to reach the diversity of many people and knows that it can do this with art as the most comfortable way; and wants to build a bridge between art and programming. Dec. The scientific side of this coding is that it is created with a programming language or languages that advance its development with logic. The creative coder needs to create an interactive art product, a living visual performance. It supports them with sound, visuals, text; it blends science and art with animations and interactivity. It is not possible to explain Creative Coding under a single title or once. As a summary for Creative coders who produce Creative Coding and living products, author and technologist Jun Wu says; &ldquo;Creative coders are people who are looking for meaning in both the creative universe and the universe of reason.&rdquo;</p>\\r\\n",
